From 883c018b4d3a26a01131f0c63eb7a774dea3fa8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mo <mo.bouss@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 00:54:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] server: add recurrent state shrink/expand for prompt
 cache (#22746)

Backport the recurrent_shrink / recurrent_expand mechanism from
BeeLlama (Anbeeld/beellama.cpp) to prevent forced full prompt
re-processing on Gated DeltaNet models (Qwen3.6, Qwen3.5, etc.).

When a recurrent/hybrid model uses prompt caching, the recurrent
state must be shrunk to 1 cell before saving/loading the cache
so the state aligns with the restored KV cache. After the cache
update, the state is expanded back to the original slot count.

Additionally, auto-detect AMD GPUs at runtime and disable context
checkpoints on non-recurrent models to prevent ROCm crashes (#20176).
Recurrent models keep checkpoints enabled since they are essential
for avoiding re-processing.

New public API:
- llama_memory_recurrent_expand / llama_memory_recurrent_shrink
- llama_context_recurrent_expand / llama_context_recurrent_shrink

Fixes: #22746, #20176, #23322
Tested: 5 consecutive agent turns, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MoE MTP,
AMD Radeon RX 7900 XTX, ROCm 7.2, zero re-processing observed.
